    <li>Drawer fronts and doors: 3/4 cherry plywood by default; sizing follows the selected frameless/face-frame front style.</li>
    <li>Current 1/16 side reveal produces 11/16 geometric overlap on a 3/4 carcass edge and a 1/8 seam between adjacent cabinet fronts.</li>
    <li>Single doors use <strong>two concealed Euro-style hinges</strong>. Hinge drilling dimensions are not generated until a hinge model is chosen.</li>
    <li>Adjustable shelves use shelf pins. Fixed mixed-cubby dividers use pocket screws.</li>
    <li>Countertops attach with screws through the flat top stretchers.</li>
    <li>No edge banding or solid-wood edge treatment is currently included.</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Open-back carcass and stretchers</h4>
  <pre>FRONT / TOP CONCEPT

  cabinet side                         cabinet side
       |                                    |
       |== front top stretcher (flat) =====|
       |                                    |
       |                                    |
       |== rear top stretcher  (flat) =====|
       |                                    |
       +========== cabinet bottom ==========+

REAR CONCEPT

       +====== rear top stretcher ======+
       |---- upper rear stretcher -------|  vertical, 4 high
       |                                 |
       |                                 |
       |---- lower rear stretcher -------|  vertical, rests on bottom
       +========== bottom ===============+</pre>
  <p>Pure drawer and single-door cabinets use birch for these carcass parts. Mixed drawer/open-cubby cabinets use cherry. Mixed cabinets keep the four stretchers and receive localized applied backs only behind open cubbies. Open-shelf cabinets use one applied full-width back instead of the two vertical rear stretchers.</p>

